meta {
  name: Report presigned URL
  type: http
  seq: 9
}

get {
  url: {{localstackBaseUrl}}/reports/presigned-url?email={{email}}&client_name={{client_name}}&date=2025-12-22&expiration=3600
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  email: {{email}}
  client_name: {{client_name}}
  date: 2025-12-22
  expiration: 3600
}

vars:pre-request {
  base_url: http://localhost:8000
  client_name: Updating
}

docs {
  # Get Report Presigned URL
  
  Generate a temporary, secure presigned URL for downloading an existing salary calculation report.
  
  ## Parameters
  - **email**: Email of the consultant (e.g., "user@example.com")
  - **client_name**: Name of the client (e.g., "ClientName")
  - **date**: Date in YYYY-MM-DD format (e.g., "2025-12-25")
  - **expiration**: Optional - URL expiration time in seconds (default: 3600 = 1 hour, max: 604800 = 7 days)
  
  ## Response
  Returns a JSON object with:
  - **url**: Pre-signed URL for downloading the report
  - **expires_in**: Expiration time in seconds
  - **bucket_key**: S3 object key (path in the bucket)
  
  ## Example Response
  ```json
  {
    "url": "https://bucket.s3.amazonaws.com/2025/12/user@example.com_ClientName_20251225.csv?X-Amz-...",
    "expires_in": 3600,
    "bucket_key": "2025/12/user@example.com_ClientName_20251225.csv"
  }
  ```
  
  ## Notes
  - The URL is temporary and will expire after the specified time
  - The report must exist in S3 (created when a calculation was saved)
  - Returns 404 if the report doesn't exist
}
